  "content": "TRACE\n\nP1. The base unit is a cell receipt. Each receipt is an append-only JSON record: `{cell_id, seq, prev_hash, before, after, cause, logical_ts, receipt_hash}`. `before` and `after` are typed value images plus schema version; `cause` is the triggering input event id or the exact dependency versions observed; `receipt_hash = SHA-256(cell_id || seq || prev_hash || canon(before) || canon(after) || canon(cause) || logical_ts)`. The double-entry book-keeping keeps both images, so reverse and reapply know the exact change without re-executing effects.\n\nP2. A cell ledger is stored as `cells/<cell_id>/receipts.log`, a sidecar `receipts.idx` mapping `seq -> byte_offset`, and `tip.json` containing the last seq, last receipt_hash, and chain length. Every append writes the receipt, fsyncs the log, then atomically rewrites `tip.json`; each new receipt must have `prev_hash` equal to the prior tip. The chain is append-only, so rewind and snapshot do not erase history; they either append new rollback records or seal a cut.\n\nP3. Single-cell rewind: given target `seq_t`, the runtime reads receipts from `seq_t+1` to the tip, verifies each `prev_hash` link and each `receipt_hash`, then applies inverse images in reverse order by setting state from each receipt’s `before`. It then appends a rollback receipt whose `before` is the current pre-rewind value, `after` is the target value, `cause = rewind_request(target_seq_t)`, and `prev_hash` is the old tip hash. The cell is now visibly at the target state while the chain remains hash-continuous.\n\nP4. Single-cell rewind invariants: the new tip must cover the rollback receipt, the restored value must equal the target receipt’s `before`, and no receipt may be deleted. Failure modes: a crash before appending the rollback leaves old state but no audit of rewind; a hash mismatch must stop before any inverse is applied; racing rewinds serialize because the second uses the first rollback as `prev_hash`, but can create surprising audit traces.\n\nP5. Organ rewind treats the organ as a write-boundary group. Each organ has `organs/<organ_id>/manifest.json` listing member cell ids and `group_receipts.log` storing `{group_txn_id, organ_id, members: {cell_id -> receipt_hash_after}, prev_group_hash, group_hash}`. To rewind to group transaction `T`, the runtime finds `T`, then rewinds every member cell to the member receipt hash recorded under `T`, and appends a group rollback record linking the previous group hash and listing restored member hashes.\n\nP6. Organ rewind invariant: after the operation, every member",
